 "notes": [
  "Source tables: registered and voters from summary table A (Äänioikeutetut ja äänestäneet sukupuolen mukaan vaalipiireittäin, pdf pages 12-14, YHTEENSÄ/total row of each constituency, which includes persons not in the domicile register in Finland); party votes from summary table C (row c, pdf page 17); rejected ballots from Table 2 (Hylätyt äänestysliput syyn mukaan vaalipiireittäin, pdf page 81, total column); electors and seats from Table 3 (Valituiksi tulleiden lukumäärä sukupuolen mukaan puolueittain ja vaalipiireittäin, pdf page 82), which agree with table C row b.",
  "Valid ballots equal the party sum in every constituency and nationally (3 177 525, as printed in Table 1 and table D); valid + rejected equals the voters total of table A in every constituency, so cast = voters (3 188 056 nationally).",
  "Electoral college of 301: by the amendment of 13.11.1981 to section 23 of the Form of Government the number of electors was raised from 300 to 301; Åland elects one elector and the other 300 are apportioned among the remaining 14 constituencies by population. Seat changes from 1978: Helsinki 31->30, Uusimaa 39->41, Turku north 20->19, Häme north 19->20.",
  "Party key ml = Keskustapuolue (KESK). Keys added: pop = Perustuslaillinen Oikeistopuolue (Konstitutionella Högerpartiet), skyp = Suomen Kansan Yhtenäisyyden Puolue (Finlands Folks Enhetsparti), al_samling = Åländsk Samling (Åland constituency only).",
  "Presidential candidates (volume text, pdf pages 8 and 18): SDP Mauno Koivisto, KOK Harri Holkeri, KESK Johannes Virolainen, SKDL Kalevi Kivistö, RKP Jan-Magnus Jansson, SMP Veikko Vennamo, SKL Raino Westerholm, LKP Helvi Sipilä. POP had no candidate but supported Mauno Koivisto; SKYP had no candidate; Åländsk Samling had no candidate but its elected elector supported Koivisto.",
  "Electoral alliances (pdf page 9): SKL+SKYP in most constituencies; SKL+SKYP+RKP in Turku north; KESK+RKP in Häme north, Kymi and Keski-Suomi; KESK+LKP in Pohjois-Karjala; KESK+SKL+RKP in Kuopio; LKP+RKP in Oulu and Lappi.",
  "Table 1 footnote: the distribution by party of votes cast in Sweden was not obtained for the Keski-Suomi and Vaasa constituencies (this affects only the municipality-level party breakdown of Table 1, not the constituency totals). The voters total includes 4 319 persons who voted at post offices in Finland while resident in Sweden (Helsinki 1 430, Turku south 438, Kymi 375, Oulu 579, Lappi 1 497).",
  "Polling days 17 and 18 January 1982. The electoral college met on 26 January 1982 and elected Mauno Koivisto on the first ballot with 167 votes."
 ],
